7829	{"artifactId":"LLD-8315a11f29fd2812-s1","entry":{"id":"migrated-LLD-8315a11f29fd2812-s1-review","actor":{"id":"insrc:daemon","kind":"agent","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-20T19:45:51.738Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"pass","summary":"review: pass","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"pass","findings":[{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.1","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"S001 designs the shared pipeline, identifier validation, provider-independent chunk limit and Ollama reviewer capability required by its upstream acceptance criteria.","evidence":"DEF §6.1 specifies ac1–ac5 for these capabilities; HLD §5.1 assigns their implementation to S001. The delivered driver sends calls serially with internalRetry:false, design-review adapters supply premise/template stages, limit.ts uses 128000 × 3, and OllamaProvider.runReviewSession uses the shared tool loop and structured emit. Document splitting and controller integration remain explicitly assigned to later Stories. [files: docs/epics/chunked-review-pipeline-every-review-E202610198315a11f/DEF.md, docs/epics/chunked-review-pipeline-every-review-E202610198315a11f/HLD.md, src/workflow/review-pipeline/driver.ts, src/workflow/review-pipeline/design-review.ts, src/workflow/review-pipeline/limit.ts, src/agent/providers/ollama.ts]","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The delivery note correctly says the pipeline and both design-review execution paths already exist in the current code.","evidence":"runReview routes design stages to runTemplateReview; otherwise it constructs premiseAdapter and executes createReviewJob/runReviewJob. runTemplateReview constructs templateAdapter and uses the same driver. The premise adapter orders extract → probe → verify, with timeoutMs:VERIFY_CALL_TIMEOUT_MS and cwd:opts.repo on daemon verification calls. [files: src/workflow/review/review.ts, src/workflow/review/template-review.ts, src/workflow/review-pipeline/design-review.ts, src/workflow/review-pipeline/driver.ts]","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.1","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"packIntoBatches is reusable with the stated signature and whole-item behavior, and its old import path remains compatible.","evidence":"The full implementation accepts items, sizeOf, budget and an optional describe callback; it tests sizeOf([item]) and throws AtomTooLargeError(describe(item), alone, budget) rather than cutting an item. The old module exports both AtomTooLargeError and packIntoBatches from '../review-pipeline/pack-into-batches.js'. [files: src/workflow/review-pipeline/pack-into-batches.ts, src/workflow/code-review/pack-into-batches.ts]","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The analyzer extraction must preserve both runShaperToolLoop and runShaper's legacy tail, because both invoke the tool loop and final structured emit.","evidence":"Both production paths call runToolLoop followed by runFinalStructuredEmit, passing configured turn/retry/output limits and tracing callbacks. The shared runToolLoop wrapper delegates to runReadOnlyToolLoop and retains analyzer-specific trace conversion and exhaustion/error handling. The design identifies both callers. [files: src/analyze/context/driver.ts]","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.1","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Older configurations lacking review.chunkTokens receive the default without requiring a bespoke migration.","evidence":"CONFIG_CATALOG declares review.chunkTokens with default:128000. Reconciliation classifies an absent leaf as 'fill' and writes cloneDefault(opt.default). Independently, readReviewChunkTokens returns DEFAULT_REVIEW_CHUNK_TOKENS when the setting or file is missing, and reviewLimitChars multiplies it by 3. [files: src/config/config-catalog.ts, src/config/reconcile.ts, src/workflow/review-pipeline/limit.ts]","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"boundaries.1","ref":"boundaries","item":"boundaries","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"S001 owns sc1–sc6; document-specific chunking and controller frame/schema changes belong to S004 and S005.","evidence":"HLD §§5.1, 5.4 and 5.5 assign exactly these responsibilities. The current design-review adapter supplies empty material and chunkCalls and explicitly rejects divided design reviews with 'dividing a design review is not available yet', consistent with its single-chunk transitional scope. S001's generic stage contracts therefore do not themselves implement S004's section material or S005's MCP frames. [files: docs/epics/chunked-review-pipeline-every-review-E202610198315a11f/HLD.md, src/workflow/review-pipeline/design-review.ts]","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.1","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"A failed premise verification is retried once and then recorded as MED not judged, while extraction failure terminates the review.","evidence":"premiseAdapter sets extract.onCallFailure='fail-review' and daemon verify.onCallFailure='record-not-judged'. applyFailure reissues before the attempt limit, then either throws ReviewCallFailedError or appends notJudged. The adapter converts failed claims into severity:'MED' findings while retaining successful answers. [files: src/workflow/review-pipeline/design-review.ts, src/workflow/review-pipeline/job.ts]","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.2","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Cancellation during a deterministic stage ends the pipeline wait and prevents committing its output.","evidence":"runStage awaits untilAborted(stage.run(job.outputs, job.snapshot, opts.signal), opts.signal), checks cancellation in the catch path and again before commit, and propagates AbortError rather than applying the stage's recording policy. [files: src/workflow/review-pipeline/job.ts]","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Each S001 acceptance criterion has a concrete test mapping supported by repository test assertions.","evidence":"Read test bodies covering ac1 prompt/order/findings/verdict parity for code, DEF and HLD reviews; ac2 missing/wrong identifiers, fresh IDs and distinct prompt hashes; ac3 the default and provider-independent configured limit; ac4 refusal replacement carrying the original evidence and excluding the refused prompt; and ac5 an Ollama session reading repository content and returning a schema-checked answer. The mapping exists; tests were inspected, not executed in this review. [files: src/workflow/review-pipeline/__tests__/single-chunk-parity.test.ts, src/workflow/review-pipeline/__tests__/pipeline-job.test.ts, src/agent/providers/__tests__/ollama-review-session.test.ts, docs/epics/chunked-review-pipeline-every-review-E202610198315a11f/DEF.md]","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"}],"counts":{"high":0,"med":0,"low":9,"unverified":0},"template":"design-spec","reviewedAt":"2026-10-20T19:45:51.738Z","model":"cli-codex:gpt-6-astra","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
